            <ArticleTitle>[Active stents: towards total prevention of restenosis?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>228-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To avoid in-stent restenosis, a new technologic approach with &quot;coated&quot; stents may deliver local cytostatic products (sirolimus, paclitaxel, tacrolimus...). At this time, present clinical studies validate the importance of these active coated stents in sub-groups of patients with diabetes, long lesions, small vessels and proximal left anterior descending coronary lesions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
